<section class="section-padding-lg bg-bg-primary dark:bg-bg-primary-dark">
    <div class="container"><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="section-intro text-left md:text-center">
            <p class="eyebrow">Why I started it</p>
            <h2>Experienced standards without the agency layer</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-text-secondary dark:text-text-secondary-dark leading-relaxed">
            <p>I have built websites for organisations ranging from small local firms to national brands. Earlier in my career, I worked as a web development project manager at one of the UK’s largest digital agencies. It showed me what strong delivery looks like—but also how agency structures, handoffs and fees can leave smaller businesses behind.</p>
            <p>I now work as a lead web developer for a major UK occupational health provider alongside running Code Craft North. That keeps me close to demanding work in performance, security and accessibility, and I bring those standards into every client project.</p>
            <p>Code Craft North is deliberately small. I take on work I can support properly, communicate directly and stay accountable for what I build. You are never passed between salespeople, designers and developers who each know only one part of the project.</p>
        </div>
        <blockquote class="plan-notice mt-8 text-lg"><strong>My aim is simple:</strong> give smaller organisations a dependable website and honest technical support without pretending they need a large agency.</blockquote>
    </div></div>
</section>

<section class="section-padding-lg bg-bg-section dark:bg-bg-section-dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">What working together feels like</p><h2>Clear, direct and grounded in the real goal</h2><p>A website should help your customers understand and trust your business. The way it is built should feel equally straightforward.</p></div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
            <article class="plan-scope-card"><h3>Clarity over complexity</h3><p>I explain what I recommend, why it matters and what it will cost before work begins.</p></article>
            <article class="plan-scope-card"><h3>Performance with purpose</h3><p>Lightweight code, accessibility and search-friendly structure support customers—not technical vanity.</p></article>
            <article class="plan-scope-card"><h3>Honest scope</h3><p>If something is included, separately quoted or unnecessary, I will say so plainly.</p></article>
            <article class="plan-scope-card"><h3>Support from the builder</h3><p>Questions and updates come back to me, so you do not have to re-explain your business each time.</p></article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-padding-lg bg-bg-primary dark:bg-bg-primary-dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">How I work</p><h2>A personal process with clear review points</h2></div>
        <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 process-list max-w-5xl mx-auto">
            <li><span>01</span><h3>Understand</h3><p>We discuss your customers, goals, constraints and what the website genuinely needs to achieve.</p></li>
            <li><span>02</span><h3>Design and build</h3><p>I shape the structure and hand-build the site, gathering your feedback at sensible points.</p></li>
            <li><span>03</span><h3>Launch and support</h3><p>I test the important details, launch clearly and provide the level of ongoing help you chose.</p></li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-padding bg-bg-section dark:bg-bg-section-dark">
    <div class="container"><div class="ownership-panel reveal">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">A practical promise</p>
            <h2>I will recommend the simplest suitable route</h2>
            <p>Sometimes that is a managed subscription. Sometimes it is a one-off build. Occasionally, the honest answer is that your current website only needs a few focused improvements.</p>
            <p>The first conversation is about understanding the problem, not steering you towards the highest invoice.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-panel__aside">
            <h3>You can expect</h3>
            <ul class="check-list">
                <li>A clear scope before work starts</li>
                <li>Direct contact with me</li>
                <li>Transparent ownership and terms</li>
                <li>No invented urgency or unnecessary upsells</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div></div>
</section>

